#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
gpu-manager.py — LLM proxy + unified GPU scheduler + VRAM lifecycle manager.

Three main functions:

1. LLM PROXY (port 8091 → 8092)
   Proxies /v1/* requests to llama.cpp backend with queue-if-unhealthy.

2. UNIFIED GPU SCHEDULER (port 8091)
   Manages declarative generation/workflow queues plus the retained legacy
   ComfyUI scheduler. ACE-Step state readers remain only for historical jobs;
   new ACE-Step admission is retired.
   GPU state machine with Qwen3.6 as the default tenant:
     - LLM_LOADED: Qwen3.6 on GPU, serving requests (default idle state)
     - DRAINING: Waiting for active LLM requests to finish before evicting
     - GPU_WORK: an admitted generation runtime using GPU
     - LLM_RELIEF: Temporary LLM restore to clear queued request backlog
     - RESTORING: Qwen3.6 reloading to GPU

   Scheduling policy:
     - Declarative queue priority plus retained ComfyUI compatibility scheduling
     - LLM pressure relief: if >=10 LLM requests queued during GPU work,
       temporarily restore LLM to clear backlog, then resume GPU work
     - Coalesce: runs all queued GPU work before restoring LLM

3. VRAM LIFECYCLE MANAGER
   Manages GPU service lifecycle and checked bundle transitions.

   The lifecycle is:
   - Before GPU work: drain active LLM requests → stop idle LLM service
   - Run GPU work: the admitted runtime owns its declared GPU resources
   - After GPU work: free models → restart idle LLM service
   - If LLM queue builds up: temporary relief cycle

Port layout:
  8091 (this service)    → external API + LLM proxy
  8092 (llama.cpp ROCm)  → Qwen3.6-35B GPU backend (evictable, default tenant)
  8188 (ComfyUI)         → image/video generation engine
  8001 (ACE-Step)        → retired backend; no new admission
  8090 (ik-llama CCD0)   → Gemma 4 E4B (DO NOT TOUCH)
"""

