# Per adversarial #4: an asyncio.Lock serialises concurrent recoveries so a
# second OOM event on the OTHER GPU does not race the first recovery's
# multi-GPU eviction check. Without this, two near-simultaneous OOMs could
# each see "other gpu is idle" and both proceed to evict — racing the same
# bundles and corrupting state.
#
# Per adversarial #5: a per-service lock prevents _force_recover_failed_service
# from being re-entered for the same service. The original code could
# recursively unload the same bundle twice (e.g. scheduler -> pipeline ->
# scheduler -> pipeline), each call wiping state the other call needed.
